        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Universal Explorer",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Finish nine regional exploration metas, including their individual zone checklists.\n\n1. Expand this meta and its nine regional Explorer achievements. Each regional meta opens zone achievements, and each zone opens its named discovery areas. Track the lowest incomplete checklist; simply uncovering most of a continent is insufficient.\n\n2. Complete Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor zone discovery lists, then Outland and Northrend. Fly or ride into each missing named area and wait for its discovery credit before moving on; descend if passing high overhead does not count. A fully revealed-looking map can still have an undiscovered small reef or settlement, particularly on Bloodmyst Isle. Use the zone achievement's checklist to find the remaining name. You generally need to discover an enemy city, not fight its leader.\n\n3. For destroyed or rebuilt areas, use the accessible Retail past phase where required: Zidormi at Darkshore 48.8, 24.5 for Teldrassil/Darnassus, at Tirisfal Glades 69.5, 62.8 for old Undercity, and beside the old Ghostlands portal at Eastern Plaguelands 53.8, 8.6 for Burning Crusade Eversong/Ghostlands. A similarly named Midnight zone does not replace the old map's discoveries. The old blood-elf and draenei starting maps restrict flight, so finish their missing areas on the ground.\n\n4. Complete Cataclysm Explorer's separate zone lists, including Hyjal, Deepholm, Vashj'ir, Uldum and Twilight Highlands. These are not all covered by the original Kalimdor/Eastern Kingdoms regional metas.\n\n5. Finish Pandaria, Draenor and Broken Isles discovery metas. In Draenor and Outland, keep their two versions of Nagrand and Shadowmoon Valley separate; discovering one does not discover the other.\n\n6. Finish Battle for Azeroth Explorer across BOTH Kul Tiras and Zandalar. Check the parent meta again and clear any remaining regional/zone entries to earn the Explorer title. Its present list ends at BfA; unrelated later-expansion exploration is not a substitute for a missing listed region.",
