    [518] = {
        achievementId = 518,
        name = "30 Exalted Reputations",
        category = "Reputation",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "30 Exalted Reputations",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Many distinct Exalted factions require several separate, sometimes time-gated grinds.\n\n1. Track this achievement and open the Reputation panel. Start with factions already near Exalted and STOP as soon as the requested counter is reached. A different character repeating the same faction is not another distinct reputation. The longer route is a choice of missing factions, not a requirement to redo every bar.\n\n2. Use your faction's six home-city reputations as an initial group: buy their reputation tabards, equip ONE and clear a suitable dungeon such as The Botanica. Confirm reputation from the first kills, then finish the run, leave and reset. Swap tabards when that faction reaches Exalted.\n\n3. REMOVE the city tabard before farming a dungeon's own faction. Add Timbermaw Hold: complete Nafien's northern Felwood introductions, kill Deadwood furbolgs near Felpaw Village and turn in batches of five Deadwood Headdress Feathers. Use the feather turn-ins to finish the bar quickly; later Retail replies report kill reputation continuing at Revered, so there is no need to stop killing while collecting feathers.\n\n4. Add Sporeggar through T'shu's Sanguine Hibiscus turn-ins inside Normal Underbog, and Cenarion Expedition through Steamvault clears. For additional reputations, combine The Diplomat, Guardian of Cenarius and The Argent Champion rather than counting duplicate factions twice.\n\n5. For the higher targets, add the Outland dungeon factions: Sha'tar in The Botanica, Lower City in Shadow Labyrinth, Consortium in Heroic Mana-Tombs and Keepers of Time in its Caverns of Time dungeons. Add raid reputations such as Violet Eye in original Karazhan and Ashtongue Deathsworn in Black Temple between resets. Stop when the achievement's distinct-faction counter reaches 30.\n\n6. Add the four remaining factions from the title routes: Kurenai OR Mag'har through Nagrand ogres and ten-war-bead hand-ins; Argent Dawn through Raymond's repeatable Annals book; Argent Crusade through its equipped Northrend tabard; and Cenarion Circle through Bor Wildmane's ten-text hand-ins. The Diplomat, Argent Champion and Guardian of Cenarius walkthroughs give the full introductions. These plus the first five steps offer 19 distinct factions. Do not count their repeated Timbermaw, Sporeggar or Expedition bars twice.\n\n7. Add Kirin Tor, Wyrmrest Accord and Knights of the Ebon Blade. Reach Friendly through their introductions, then buy their tabards from Alvareaux upstairs in Northrend Dalaran's Violet Citadel, Cielstrasza atop Wyrmrest Temple, and Mynx at the UNLOCKED Shadow Vault. Equip one PHYSICAL tabard and clear Normal Halls of Lightning; leave, reset and repeat to Exalted before swapping to the next. Use the Northrend Vanguard faction guides if a vendor is phased. Argent Crusade was already counted in the previous step.\n\n8. Add your faction's Alliance Vanguard OR Horde Expedition and its separate Silver Covenant OR Sunreavers reputation. REMOVE championing tabards and clear original Wrath Heroics such as Utgarde Keep or Gundrak, checking the actual bars after kills. Rotate unsaved Heroics after boss kills. For the Covenant/Sunreavers, also complete the Argent Tournament's mounted introduction, Aspirant and Valiant promotions, then its unlocked dailies. These are two distinct faction bars; the five-city Champion title is not required just to earn their reputation.\n\n9. Add Sons of Hodir. Start They Took Our Men! with Gretchen Fizzlespark in K3, then finish the Brunnhildar/Thorim chain through Mending Fences. Loot Slag Covered Metal and finish The Refiner's Fire and A Spark of Hope. Continue until Dun Niffelem is friendly and Lillehoff offers repeatable Relics of Ulduar hand-ins. Buy or farm relics and repeat those hand-ins to Exalted, supplementing with unlocked dailies. Do not buy a large stock before opening the turn-in.\n\n10. Add The Kalu'ak through its Northrend stories, then three dailies: Utaik's Preparing for the Worst at Kaskala in Borean Tundra, Trapper Mau'i's Planning for the Future at Moa'ki Harbor, Dragonblight, and Anuniaq's The Way to His Heart... at Kamagua, Howling Fjord. The last needs the Kamagua/Scalawag Point pirate introduction. Complete all three after each daily reset until Exalted; there is no dungeon-championing Kalu'ak tabard.\n\n11. Add ONE Sholazar faction, preferably Oracles if you want its optional egg rewards. At Pitch, take Playing Along from Tracker Gekgek and finish the Frenzyheart/Oracle story to A Hero's Burden. In Artruis's cave, damage the lich carefully until BOTH prisoners are released; kill Zepik and save Jaloot for Oracles. Complete Jaloot's Hand of the Oracles AND Return of the Friendly Dryskin, then do all three Rainspeaker Canopy dailies after resets to Exalted. Do not switch allegiance while finishing this bar; Frenzyheart is an alternative, not a second simultaneous Exalted faction.\n\n12. Add Honor Hold OR Thrallmar by repeatedly clearing NORMAL Shattered Halls in Hellfire Citadel, Outland. Kill the trash as well as the bosses, leave, reset outside and repeat. Its Normal kills continue beyond the caps of the lower-level Hellfire dungeons. No Flamewrought Key or old attunement is required. Count only your faction's bar.\n\n13. Add Sha'tari Skyguard. Start Threat from Above with Yuula beside Shattrath's flight master and follow To Skettis to Blackwind Landing. Farm Skettis arakkoa for Shadow Dust and exchange six at a time with Severin for Elixir of Shadows; keep it active to see time-lost arakkoa. Follow the Almanac/Hazzik introduction in Flying High Over Skettis to unlock the four descendant summons and Terokk. Repeat kills, dust exchanges and those summons to Exalted; the bombing/escort dailies supplement the repeatable farm.\n\n14. Add Netherwing. Start Mordenai's Kindness in OUTLAND Shadowmoon Valley, follow the airborne Neltharaku's drake-rescue chain, free Karynaku from Zuluhed, and finish Ally of the Netherwing. Continue Blood Oath of the Netherwing and In Service of the Illidari to the disguised island camp. Finish The Great Netherwing Egg Hunt to unlock repeatable egg hand-ins, then combine eggs with the available camp/mine dailies and each rank promotion until Exalted. The Netherwing guide has the full unlock; an egg bought before those quests is not an unlocked turn-in.\n\n15. Add ONE Shattrath allegiance. Complete Khadgar's City of Light introduction and choose Aldor OR Scryers. Aldor: Adyen takes Marks of Kil'jaeden to Honored, then Marks of Sargeras; Ishanah also takes Fel Armaments. Scryers: Fyalenn takes Firewing Signets to Honored, then Sunfury Signets; Voren'thal also takes Arcane Tomes. Farm or buy the appropriate items and repeat hand-ins to Exalted. Raising one side lowers the other, so do not switch for this count route.\n\n16. Add Shattered Sun Offensive on the ORIGINAL Burning Crusade Isle of Quel'Danas. Shattrath's island portal provides access. Clear NORMAL original Magisters' Terrace, use the exit orb, reset outside and repeat; these kills can finish Exalted. The harbor dailies are optional extra reputation. Do not enter Midnight's replacement dungeon or pay the separate title donation as if it were a reputation prerequisite.\n\n17. Add Scale of the Sands and Ashen Verdict. For Scale, enter the original Battle for Mount Hyjal raid inside Caverns of Time; start Jaina's two wave sequences, then Thrall's two, and finish Archimonde. Repeat full clears after weekly resets. For Ashen Verdict, kill Icecrown Citadel's entrance trash, leave Marrowgar ALIVE, exit and reset for repeat trash runs; activate floor traps for extra Deathbound Wards. Killing Marrowgar saves the raid, so use weekly full clears instead if already saved. Observe the instance-entry limit.\n\n18. Add five Cataclysm factions: Guardians of Hyjal, Earthen Ring, Therazane, Ramkahen, and your faction's Wildhammer OR Dragonmaw. Finish their zone introductions to Friendly, especially Deepholm's story for Therazane, then buy each mapped quartermaster's tabard. Equip one and clear original Cataclysm HEROICS such as Stonecore; rotate unsaved Heroics and return after daily resets, swapping tabards at Exalted. Check the first kills award the chosen faction. Friendly unlocks the tabard, not the Exalted milestone. This adds five separate bars rather than five appearances of one bar.\n\n19. For the fortieth distinct faction, add Brood of Nozdormu in the TEMPLE of Ahn'Qiraj, not the Ruins used for Cenarion Circle. Kill trash until its reputation stops at 2,999/3,000 Neutral, saving Qiraji Lord's Insignias and Ancient Qiraji Artifacts. Beyond that, use boss kills and the friendly dragons' item hand-ins near the raid entrance: Mortal Champions takes insignias, while artifacts start their own turn-in. Repeat after weekly resets. Classic Timewalking commendations are an optional badge-funded alternative while their vendor is active. This faction starts Hated, so a Neutral-to-Exalted token total is insufficient from scratch.",
        stepCount = 19,
        waypoints = {
