    [878] = {
        achievementId = 878,
        name = "One That Didn't Get Away",
        category = "Professions",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "One That Didn't Get Away",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - The qualifying rare fish is random and may require many casts or scenario attempts.\n\n1. Track the achievement: you need ONE of its qualifying rare fish, not every fish on the list. Learn Fishing and clear bag space before starting. You must personally fish up AND LOOT the catch; seeing it in the loot window or buying someone else's fish is insufficient.\n\n2. Visit Chromie at the TOP of Wyrmrest Temple in Dragonblight. Complete The Day That Chromie Dies, then Rewind, to unlock repeatable attempts at The Deaths of Chromie. This is the Legion scenario, not Chromie Time levelling. If Andorhal is not yet available, do the Emerald Dragonshrine unlock below.\n\n3. Inside the scenario, complete the Emerald Dragonshrine attack around 63.5, 73.2: collect 24 Emeraldine Plumes and 30 Twisted Fibers, make three Nightmare-Catchers and use them to defeat the six Dream Tormentors. Defeat Thalas Vylethorn by the skull/hand statue, loot his Gleaming Chronoshard and turn it in to unlock the Andorhal portal.\n\n4. Start another attempt, speak to Chromie to begin, then take the Andorhal portal on your left. Leave the burning building and reach the river. Fish OPEN WATER for a 32 Pound Catfish; no school is needed. A September 2026 reply identifies water beside the bridge around 39.25, 71.25 on the SCENARIO's Andorhal map.\n\n5. Keep fishing until the scenario timer expires, then restart and return through the unlocked portal. It stays unlocked between attempts. The smaller catfish do not stack, so empty bags between runs and keep Auto Loot enabled. Loot the 32 Pound Catfish when it appears and check credit immediately. Reports range from a few casts to many full attempts; there is no guaranteed number of runs.\n\n6. For an outdoor route without scenario unlocks, fish open water at Stonebull Lake in Mulgore, around 44.3, 61.1, for a 15 Pound Mud Snapper. Alliance characters should keep clear of Bloodhoof Village's Horde guards. Stay at a safe part of the lake rather than entering the village.\n\n7. Alternatively, fish open water at Crystal Lake in Elwynn Forest, beside the memorial island around 48.47, 65.61, for the same 15 Pound Mud Snapper. A March 2026 comment and its August reply confirm this route. These outdoor stops are alternatives to Andorhal; stop as soon as one qualifying catch awards the achievement.",
        stepCount = 7,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 115, x = 0.599, y = 0.547, step = 2, label = "Wyrmrest Temple - Chromie is on top" },
            {
                mapID = 897,
                x = 0.635,
                y = 0.732,
                step = 3,
                label = "Emerald Dragonshrine - unlock Andorhal",
                mapName = "The Deaths of Chromie - Dragonblight",
            },
            {
                mapID = 899,
                x = 0.3925,
                y = 0.7125,
                step = 4,
                label = "Scenario Andorhal - fish by the bridge",
                mapName = "The Deaths of Chromie - Andorhal",
            },
            {
                mapID = 7,
                x = 0.44299999999999995,
                y = 0.611,
                step = 6,
                label = "Stonebull Lake - alternative 15 Pound Mud Snapper",
