    [1017] = {
        achievementId = 1017,
        name = "Can I Keep Him?",
        category = "Collections",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Can I Keep Him?",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Easy - A small batch of permanent vendor pets or racial mounts meets the target.\n\n1. Open the Pet Journal and track this achievement. Collect 1 DIFFERENT pet species; three copies of one species do not become three unique pets. Stop when the requested count is reached. Use the nearby vendor batch first, and the later batches only for entries you still need.\n\n2. Alliance vendor batch: buy Bombay, Cornish Rex, Orange Tabby and Silver Tabby cats from Donni Anthania in Elwynn Forest; both owl species from Shylenai in Stormwind's northern refugee area; Snowshoe Rabbit from Yarlyn Amberstill in Dun Morogh; and Blue, White and Yellow Moths from Sixx in the Exodar. These are ten different species. USE every carrier/egg to learn the pet; a closed carrier in your bags is not collected.\n\n3. Horde vendor batch: buy Black Kingsnake, Brown Snake and Crimson Snake from Xan'tish, who walks through Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits; Prairie Dog from Halpa in Thunder Bluff; and Golden, Red and Silver Dragonhawks from Jilanne in the BURNING CRUSADE version of Eversong Woods. Use the past Quel'Thalas phase to reach Jilanne. Pets learned on an eligible faction alt join the same account journal, so no old neutral-Auction-House transfer is needed.\n\n4. Neutral vendor batch: visit Dealer Rashaad beside the Stormspire inn in Netherstorm (43.5, 35.2). Buy missing Brown Rabbit, Cockroach, Crimson Snake, Mana Wyrmling, Red Moth, Senegal, Siamese Cat and Blue Dragonhawk Hatchling. Crimson Snake overlaps Xan'tish's stock, so skip a duplicate rather than counting it twice.\n\n5. Add Cockatiel from Narkk in Booty Bay (42.6, 69.2, Cape of Stranglethorn). For Ancona Chicken, go to Tirth's Haunt in southeastern Thousand Needles (85.4, 91.4), right-click the running chicken named Plucky Johnson and buy while he is human; interact again if he transforms back. Do not follow the old Magus Tirth vendor directions to the submerged pre-Cataclysm race track. The combined vendor batches can supply 26 different species.\n\n6. For the remaining count, browse Auction House > Battle Pets and compare the species with your Journal's Not Collected list before buying. Pick inexpensive LEVEL 1 cages you can learn; a higher-level caged pet can be unusable until you have already levelled a pet that high yourself. Loot purchases from mail, right-click each cage to learn it, then check the achievement. Rarity and breed are irrelevant when collecting a new species.\n\n7. For a gold-saving alternative, learn Battle Pet Training from Audrey Burnhep in Stormwind (69.2, 25.0) or Varzok in Orgrimmar (52.6, 58.8). Put a battle-ready pet in the first team slot and enable Track Pets. Start against low-level wild pets around Goldshire in Elwynn Forest or Razor Hill in Durotar, then follow the trainer's introductory battles as your team levels.\n\n8. To capture a missing wild species, start its pet battle, reduce its health below 35% without killing it, then use Trap until successful and finish the battle. Look for green paw markers and check the species tooltip before fighting. Capture new names as you move through zones; an extra breed or colour of the SAME species is not another entry. Buying pets is optional if you prefer to complete the remaining collection through captures.\n\n9. Continue until the counter reaches 1. Learning the item is essential; merely keeping an unused carrier or cage in your bags is insufficient.",
        stepCount = 9,
        waypoints = {
