        category = "Collections",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Twenty-Five Tabards",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Collect a larger batch of permanent pets, mounts or tabards from the mapped routes.\n\n1. Open Appearances > Tabards and track this achievement. Learn 25 distinct qualifying appearances, checking the counter after each purchase. Stop as soon as the target is met; the later batches below are alternatives for larger collections. Extra copies of one tabard are not extra entries.\n\n2. Start with your faction's six basic city tabards from the mapped quartermasters; the Ambassador guide uses the same vendor route. Buy the inexpensive silver-priced city tabards rather than paying Champion's Seals at the Argent Tournament. Add a standard Guild Tabard from Rebecca Laughlin in Stormwind or Garyl in Orgrimmar. Equip purchased tabards to make their appearances permanent. These provide up to seven entries.\n\n3. Add the four Northrend tabards at Friendly reputation: Argent Crusade from Aliocha Segard, Kirin Tor from Archmage Alvareaux, Wyrmrest Accord from Cielstrasza on top of Wyrmrest Temple, and Ebon Blade from Duchess Mynx. Quest for a missing Friendly reputation; Mynx also needs the Shadow Vault quest hub unlocked. This brings the suggested collection to eleven.\n\n4. Add five Cataclysm tabards at Friendly: Guardians of Hyjal from Whitecloud inside Nordrassil inn; Earthen Ring from Arok in the Silver Tide Hollow underwater cave; Ramkahen from Abasi; Therazane from D'lom; and your faction's Wildhammer or Dragonmaw tabard from Craw MacGraw or Grot Deathblow. Complete the corresponding zone introductions if the faction/vendor is still locked, especially Therazane's Deepholm chain. These bring the suggested total to sixteen.\n\n5. For five more, finish Cenarion Expedition, Sporeggar, Lower City, Sha'tar and Keepers of Time reputations to Exalted, then buy their tabards from Rebecca or Garyl's eligible stock. Use the individual reputation guides for the grinds. Sporeggar's tabard costs ten Glowcaps, so gather those mushrooms around Sporeggar or check the Auction House before visiting the shared vendor. Existing Outland tabards you already own can replace any missing choice.\n\n6. If still short, Rebecca or Garyl sells four old PvP tabards: Private's Tabard/Scout's Tabard, Knight's Colors/Stone Guard's Herald, Stormpike/Frostwolf Battle Tabard and Silverwing/Warsong Battle Tabard. Their current listed prices are one, one, ten and ten Marks of Honor respectively. Buy missing ones, equip them and keep each permanent unlock. With the preceding batches, these supply a complete 25-tabard route without a retired event reward or random drop.\n\n7. At 25, check your mail for Tabard of the Achiever. If already earned on the account, speak to a tabard vendor about replacing it on this character.",
