    [1999] = {
        achievementId = 1999,
        name = "10 Cooking Awards",
        category = "Professions",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "10 Cooking Awards",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Repeat daily quests or the confirmed repeatable award turn-in.\n\n1. Learn Cooking and visit your faction's cooking daily quest giver in NORTHREND Dalaran: Katherine Lee at 40.3, 66.1 for Alliance, or Awilo Lon'gomba at 70.0, 38.9 for Horde. Train the required Cooking tier/skill if the offered quest is unavailable for lack of skill.\n\n2. Accept TODAY'S offered daily, collect or cook exactly what it requests and turn it in. Only one of this Dalaran rotation is available per day; you cannot complete all five variants each day. Mustard Dogs! awards two rather than one. Claim the awards, open the Small Spice Bag and inspect the achievement counter.\n\n3. Add one capital-city cooking daily on the SAME character that day: Robby Flay in Stormwind (50.6, 71.6) or Marogg in Orgrimmar (56.6, 62.6). The capital-city rotation is separate from Northrend Dalaran's. Switching between your faction's three capital quest givers does not provide three capital dailies; inspect their offered rewards before choosing if you want the two-award variant.\n\n4. For a supplement, do Marcia Chase's Northrend fishing daily and open its Bag of Fishing Treasures. If it contains Waterlogged Recipe, right-click the quest-starting item and deliver it to Christi Stockton in One More Glass (53.4, 33.2, NORTHREND Dalaran) for five Epicurean's Awards. Learn Northrend Cooking first. The current unbound quest item can also be bought from the Auction House; compare its price before buying several.\n\n5. Waterlogged Recipe is repeatable: complete its hand-in before accepting the next copy. Check the counter after the first one. Otherwise return for the cooking dailies after each daily reset until you have earned 10 awards. The target counts awards earned, so a two-award daily or five-award recipe can advance it by more than one.\n\n6. Spend earned awards on needed recipes if desired; the achievement tracks accumulation rather than requiring all awards in your wallet at once. Save enough for a Chef's Hat separately if you want that purchase.",
