    [2536] = {
        achievementId = 2536,
        name = "Mountain o' Mounts",
        category = "Collections",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Mountain o' Mounts",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Combine many mount purchases and separate reputation grinds; tournament unlocks add daily resets if needed.\n\n1. Track this achievement on the character with your highest mount counter. The target is 100 mounts usable for this milestone. In the Mount Journal, enable Not Collected to identify missing colours; its overall total can include opposite-faction variants that do not add to this counter. Stop the route as soon as you reach your target.\n\n2. Start with racial mount vendors. A character of the vendor's own race can normally buy its mounts without an Exalted grind; learn them on an eligible permanent alt, then log back into your collector. Other races need Exalted with that city. If a vendor refuses, check the character's race, reputation and item requirements; for example, Lightforged Draenei do not receive the ordinary Draenei exemption.\n\n3. ALLIANCE route: Katie Hunter at Eastvale Logging Camp sells six horses; Unger Statforth at Menethil Harbor adds Black Stallion. Veron Amberstill sells six rams and Milli Featherwhistle seven mechanostriders in Dun Morogh. In northern Stormwind, buy seven sabers from Lelanai and two mountain horses from Astrid Langstrump. Torallius, just outside Exodar's main exit, sells six elekks. These batches offer 35 different mounts; buy only colours you have not learned.\n\n4. HORDE route: buy seven wolves from Ogunaro Wolfrunner and two trikes from Kall Worthaton in Orgrimmar; six raptors from Zjolnir in Sen'jin Village; six kodos from Harb Clawhoof in Bloodhoof Village; seven skeletal horses from Zachariah Post at Brill; and seven hawkstriders from Winaestra at Thuron's Livery. These batches also offer 35 mounts. Use Zidormi's past Tirisfal/Quel'Thalas phases if the old vendors are absent. Buying the other faction's counterpart colours does not double your achievement progress.\n\n5. Add twelve dragon turtles: six normal colours and their six Great versions. Alliance uses Old Whitenose beside Stormwind's lake; Horde uses Turtlemaster Odai in Orgrimmar. Use a Pandaren of your faction, or earn Exalted with Tushui/Huojin by wearing the nearby quartermaster's tabard in eligible dungeons. Check the first reputation gain before repeating runs. Different item IDs teaching the SAME turtle are not extra mounts; check Already Known before buying.\n\n6. Visit Mei Francis in NORTHREND Dalaran (58.0, 42.4). Buy your seven ordinary gryphon/wind rider colours if missing, then compare the Armored Brown Bear and Armored Snowy Gryphon/Armored Blue Wind Rider with your remaining budget. You do not need the expensive Traveler's Tundra Mammoth. Use every reins item to LEARN it; unused items in your bags do not build the learned-mount counter.\n\n7. For eight more mounts, reach Exalted with Kurenai or Mag'har in OUTLAND Nagrand. Finish their introductory quests, then kill Nagrand ogres and turn in Obsidian Warbeads using The Diplomat route. Buy all four Riding Talbuk colours AND all four War Talbuk colours from Trader Narasu in Telaar or Provisioner Nasela in Garadar. These eight do not require Halaa battle tokens.\n\n8. For eleven more, reach Sha'tari Skyguard Exalted and buy Grella's five nether rays at Blackwind Landing; complete the Netherwing introduction and reputation grind for six Netherwing drake colours. The first drake is a quest reward; buy the other five from Drake Dealer Hurlunk on Netherwing Ledge. Use their individual mount guides for the unlock quests. Only one free reward does not mean only one colour can be learned.\n\n9. For the remaining gap to 100, choose missing vendor batches instead of waiting for rare drops: five faction war mounts from Lieutenant Karter/Raider Bork (Marks of Honor); Cenarion War Hippogryph from Fedryen Swiftspear at Cenarion Expedition Exalted; Red Drake from Cielstrasza at Wyrmrest Accord Exalted; two mammoths from Lillehoff after the Sons of Hodir introduction and required reputations; and two ordinary riding camels from Blacksmith Abasi at Ramkahen Exalted. Read current prices: old battleground marks, Justice Points and Stone Keeper's Shards are obsolete. Check the individual mount guides before starting a reputation from scratch.\n\n10. The Argent Tournament supplies another large permanent batch if you still need mounts. Start with Justicar Mariel Trueheart at the Icecrown tournament grounds. Complete the jousting training, Aspirant and Valiant dailies through your city's Champion trial; keep doing Champion dailies for Champion's Seals. Champion the other cities in turn to open their quartermasters. Prioritise each city's mount costing five seals plus gold before saving for its 100-seal mount. This unlock takes daily resets; the vendors are inside the faction pavilions at the mapped grounds.\n\n11. Recheck the achievement after learning each batch. If progress stalls despite new mounts, log the character with your highest usable count, open its Mount Journal and learn another missing mount if necessary. At 50, inspect the Journal for Albino Drake; at 100, inspect it for your faction's Dragonhawk. Later comments report these rewards are added directly, so do not wait only for a letter.",
        stepCount = 11,
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 37, x = 0.84, y = 0.655, step = 3, label = "Katie Hunter - six horses, Eastvale Logging Camp" },
