        category = "Dungeons",
        sourceType = "Achievement",
        source = "Looking For Multitudes",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Finish repeated Random Heroics with qualifying random teammates.\n\n1. Open Group Finder > Dungeon Finder and choose an available RANDOM HEROIC queue. Selecting a specific Heroic dungeon or walking through a dungeon portal does not satisfy this queue requirement.\n\n2. Queue alone for the most random teammates per completion, or bring a friend if that makes queuing easier. You and players already in your party when you queue do not count as random teammates. Queue afresh after a completed run; continuing with the same assembled party can stop it adding new random teammates.\n\n3. Finish the dungeon, including its final boss. Repeat random Heroics until the achievement counter reaches 100 random players. A full run with four qualifying teammates can add four, so this counts PLAYERS rather than requiring 100 separate dungeons.\n\n4. If Random Heroic is absent, inspect a Heroic in the Specific Dungeons list to see its current level and equipment requirements, meet those requirements, then return to the RANDOM queue. Changing your portrait's dungeon difficulty does not turn a Random Normal queue into Random Heroic.\n\n5. At 100 random players, check your mail for the Perky Pug reward and learn it. Looking For Many, the earlier 50-player milestone, awards the Patient title.",
