        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Complete a large species checklist with some limited or sparse spawns.\n\n1. Unlock pet trapping and track this Safari. You need the exact listed species, not a particular color or quality. Catching a rare is optional; capture any available quality before waiting for an upgrade.\n\n2. Work through the missing species zone by zone. Use each map's labelled search areas and the species' own guide where available. Lower a chosen wild pet below 35%, trap it, then win the full encounter. Inspect backline names too; only one opponent can be captured per battle.\n\n3. Plan the limited spawns early: Qiraji Guardling appears during summer in Silithus, Snowy Owl during winter in Winterspring, and Silithid Hatchling during a Tanaris sandstorm. Minfernal in Felwood can require repeated searches. Use an earlier accessible Retail phase when the zone has changed.\n\n4. Checklist: Adder; Alpine Hare; Ash Lizard; Black Rat; Biletoad; Chicken; Cockroach; Creepy Crawly; Crystal Spider; Death's Head Cockroach; Diemetradon Hatchling; Elfin Rabbit; Fire Beetle; Forest Moth; Gazelle Fawn; Gold Beetle; Hare; Horny Toad; Infected Squirrel; Locust; Mac Frog; Minfernal; Mountain Skunk; Nether Faerie Dragon; Oasis Moth; Prairie Dog; Rabbit; Rat; Ravager Hatchling; Roach; Rock Viper; Sand Kitten; Scorpid; Shimmershell Snail; Sidewinder; Silky Moth; Small Frog; Snowy Owl; Spider; Spiny Lizard; Squirrel; Stone Armadillo; Stripe-Tailed Scorpid; Tainted Moth; Toad; Topaz Shale Hatchling; Turquoise Turtle; Twilight Iguana; Venomspitter Hatchling; Alpine Chipmunk; Amethyst Shale Hatchling; Bat; Beetle; Carrion Rat; Cheetah Cub; Coral Snake; Crested Owl; Darkshore Cub; Desert Spider; Dung Beetle; Emerald Boa; Fire-Proof Roach; Frog; Giraffe Calf; Grey Moth; Horned Lizard; Infected Fawn; Leopard Scorpid; Long-Tailed Mole; Maggot; Mountain Cottontail; Mouse; Nordrassil Wisp; Parrot; Qiraji Guardling; Rabid Nut Varmint 5000; Rattlesnake; Red-Tailed Chipmunk; Robo-Chick; Rusty Snail; Scarab Hatchling; Sea Gull; Shore Crab; Silithid Hatchling; Skunk; Snake; Spawn of Onyxia; Spiky Lizard; Spotted Bell Frog; Stinkbug; Strand Crab; Tainted Cockroach; Tainted Rat; Tol'vir Scarab; Tree Python; Twilight Beetle; Twilight Spider; Water Snake.\n\n5. Check every criterion before leaving a region. For an unexpectedly missing entry, verify the exact species name and a completed capture. Do not release a valuable owned pet just because an old launch-bug comment suggested doing so. Return during a required season or weather window rather than treating those species as permanently unobtainable.",
