        difficultyReason = "A sequential account unlock and a team of trained battle pets are required.",
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A sequential account unlock and a team of trained battle pets are required.\n\n1. Start with Audrey Burnhep in Stormwind (Alliance) or Varzok in Orgrimmar (Horde). Complete the introductory healing, leveling and capture lessons, then accept each next tamer quest after winning. Use a Horde character to accept this continent's early handoffs; an opposite-faction character cannot take every handoff.\n\n2. Defeat Zunta at 44,28.8. Bring Beast and Mechanical attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n3. Defeat Dagra the Fierce at 58.6,53. Bring Beast and Mechanical attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n4. Defeat Analynn at 20.2,29.6. Bring Magic, Flying and Beast attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n5. Defeat Zonya the Sadist at 59.6,71.6. Bring Mechanical and Beast attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n6. Defeat Merda Stronghoof at 57.2,45.8. Bring Aquatic, Flying and Beast attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n7. Defeat Cassandra Kaboom at 39.6,79.2. Bring Elemental attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n8. Defeat Traitor Gluk at 59.6,49.6. Bring Humanoid, Beast and Mechanical attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n9. Defeat Grazzle the Great at 53.8,74.8. Bring Humanoid attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n10. Defeat Kela Grimtotem at 31.8,32.8. Bring Mechanical and Beast attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n11. Defeat Zoltan at 40,56.6. Bring Dragonkin and Elemental attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n12. Defeat Elena Flutterfly at 46,60.6. Bring Dragonkin, Magic and Humanoid attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n13. Defeat Stone Cold Trixxy at 65.6,64.6. Bring Magic, Mechanical and Humanoid attacks to counter this team. Heal between battles and use rare-quality, appropriately leveled pets; your character's combat level does not improve pet attacks. Accept or complete the matching tamer quest before moving on.\n\n14. Turn in the continent assignment, defeat its grand master and accept the return to the capital. The grand-master introduction is distinct from the later repeatable daily. In Uldum, use Zidormi's earlier phase if needed; in the Vale use the earlier Pandaria phase for Aki, and look inside the Kota Peak cave for Yon. Check the achievement's individual trainer ticks before repeating battles.",
